{"agent":"Monster3-fix-B6341fe42ca-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"When `output.status_fix_tasks_in_headline` is true, the new suffix says only “fix tasks included” and omits the abandoned count. For example, with 15 live tasks (5 normal + 5 fix + 5 abandoned), 8 done among the live/fix tasks, and `abandoned=5`, the line becomes `Progress: tasks 8/15 ... · live tasks, fix tasks included`; the 5 abandoned tasks are excluded from the task denominator but are not disclosed, so the operator cannot reconcile the Progress line with status JSON or STATUS.md totals. The false branch explicitly discloses abandoned tasks, so the true branch should also disclose them (or include them); otherwise the change leaves the exact kind of unexplained total mismatch it is meant to fix.","digest":"79b47d11ab599402","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/progress_line.py:_progress","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/progress_line.py:_progress"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The added `status_completed_shown` row states that `0` “lists all” completions, but the existing `allow_full` row in the same output-caps table states that setting `allow_full=false` “stops 0 lifting a cap.” Given `allow_full=false` and `status_completed_shown=0`, the documentation gives contradictory behavior: the new row promises an uncapped `Completed` list while the general cap contract says a zero cap must not lift. This makes the new knob’s contract unreliable, which is exactly the kind of ambiguity this change is supposed to eliminate.","digest":"9fda1bfb80e227d2","family":"alibaba","location":"docs/ddflow/output-caps.md:25","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"docs/ddflow/output-caps.md:25"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"The new expected STATUS.md by-state line is arithmetically wrong for the fixture: it asserts the body contains `2 done + 1 running + 0 review + 0 not started + 0 abandoned = 7`, but those bucket counts sum to `3`, not `7`. The original assertion for the same fixture had `4 open` tasks, so this expected line either drops those four tasks from the displayed buckets while still claiming the total is `7`, or it will fail once the export correctly puts them into a bucket and sums to the total. That directly contradicts the change's stated invariant that every bucket sums to the reported total.","digest":"c02cec74834808d9","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:331","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_export_docs_a.py:331"},{"chunk":8,"detail":"The assertion `assert \"= 4\" in out` does not verify that the reconciled total is exactly four; it is a plain substring check. Given a status output containing any occurrence of `= 4` followed by more characters, such as `total tasks = 40` or an unrelated `bug count = 41`, the test still passes even though the headline does not reconcile to four task records. The same weak check is repeated at line 77, so the test does not reliably tie the printed buckets to the total.","digest":"575e5b2f6872d0cd","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_status_task_count_labels.py:65","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_status_task_count_labels.py:65"},{"chunk":8,"detail":"After completing `T2`, the test checks only that the new status contains `\"2 of 2 live tasks done\"` and never rechecks the reconciled total. If the post-completion status regresses to `2 of 2 live tasks done (1 abandoned and 1 fix tasks listed separately) = 2`, the assertion still passes, so a bug where the total drops from the four records to the live pair after completion would not be caught.","digest":"ae0eb5ed8cae5d63","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_status_task_count_labels.py:83","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_status_task_count_labels.py:83"},{"chunk":9,"detail":"The fixture creates tasks directly in the event log with a phase parent but without the required dependency/wave metadata. For example, `log.append(\"task.added\", \"D00\", {\"title\": ..., \"parent\": \"P1\", \"globs\": [...]})` (and the same for `A0`, `F1`, `F2`, `R1`, `R2`, and the blocked `K*` tasks) has no `wave:N` tag and no `no-deps` tag for tasks with no prerequisites. This violates [r-task-phase-needs-wave], which says every task must state its dependencies in `needs` and carry a `wave:N` tag (or `no-deps` when it has no prerequisite).","digest":"892720424bd99a2e","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_status_totals.py:36","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_status_totals.py:36"}],"chunks_total":9,"coverage":"8/9 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":40334,"diff_sha":"6685756503e657ebfae924b4d92d952bf2c8cbe0677dbfd4e8dd628f54d62c11","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B6341fe42ca","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1404.3,"excluded_bytes":1058,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":6,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"27c0941ba299c1ad","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B6341fe42ca.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T034159Z-037c8d33.jsonl","reason":"1 of 9 chunk(s) not reviewed:\n  chunk 3/9 (ddflow/core/progress/totals.py): TRUNCATED: the model consumed all 64000 tokens (64000 of them reasoning) before emitting any answer. This is UNAVAILABLE, not a clean review. If the model's vendor recommends a temperature, check the server applies it ([[reviewer]].temperature sets one explicitly). Otherwise raise [[reviewer]].max_tokens, or lower [[reviewer]].max_chunk_chars so each chunk needs less thinking. (retried, still unreviewed)","review_degraded":[{"at":1794542724.1849072,"family":"google","gate":"ru